# route 44.32.58.0/24 -- exists in RADB, maintained by ARDC. Verify only.
#
# Live object on 2026-09-10 (whois -h whois.radb.net 44.32.58.0/24):

route:          44.32.58.0/24
origin:         AS215520
descr:          KN4LJL
mnt-by:         MAINT-ARDC
last-modified:  2026-04-17T20:28:15Z
source:         RADB

# Why the operator does not create this object anywhere:
#
#   RADB   The object above is generated by ARDC's portal from the 44Net
#          allocation record. `mnt-by: MAINT-ARDC` means only ARDC can change
#          it. A second RADB object under an operator maintainer would need a
#          paid RADB maintainer and would be a duplicate; if the origin ever
#          changes, ask ARDC (ardc-request.md, section 1).
#
#   ARIN   ARIN's IRR only accepts route objects from the ARIN Online org that
#          holds the block (ARDC, NET-44-0-0-0-1). Not available to the
#          operator. ARDC may create one in addition to RADB; harmless.
#
#   RIPE   A `route:` for non-RIPE space can only land in RIPE-NONAUTH, which
#          RIPE stopped accepting new objects into (2018) and which upstreams
#          and IX route servers no longer honour. Do not try.
#
#   ALTDB  Free, self-service and therefore worthless as proof of
#          authorisation; Vultr and modern filters (bgpq4 with default
#          sources, IRRd 4 "authoritative source" preference, RPKI-IRR
#          conflict filtering) prefer RADB/ARIN. Only create an ALTDB copy if
#          an upstream explicitly requires an object under the operator's own
#          maintainer; wording would be:
#
#            route:      44.32.58.0/24
#            descr:      AS215520 anycast /24 (ARDC 44Net allocation KN4LJL)
#            origin:     AS215520
#            mnt-by:     MAINT-AS215520     # would have to be registered at ALTDB first
#            source:     ALTDB
#
# Vultr: BYOIP onboarding accepts RADB objects (infra/providers/vultr/facts.yaml
# byoip.irr.accepted) and, if none matched, would auto-create one under
# MAINT-AS20473. The ARDC object already matches, so nothing will be created.
#
# Verify:
#   whois -h whois.radb.net -- '-i origin AS215520'
#   scripts/netcheck   (row radb:route:44.32.58.0/24 must be OK)
